WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
OSHA 10 is not optional. You need this to work on most commercial job sites.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Electrical safety for HVAC technicians: lockout/tagout procedures, arc flash
awareness, proper use of insulated tools, and working near energized equipment.
OSHA requires de-energization and LOTO before working on electrical systems. If

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Arc Flash: Electrical explosion through air causing severe burns. Proper PPE and
de-energization prevent it.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
GFCI: Ground Fault Circuit Interrupter. Trips in milliseconds if current leaks
to ground. Required on construction sites.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Electrical accidents are the third leading
cause of construction death. LOTO saves lives.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Always LOTO before electrical work. And — Verify zero
energy with YOUR meter

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
